<BaseLayout adsEnabled={false} title="Editorial Policy | Food Supply Crisis Report" description="Editorial and sourcing standards for Food Supply Crisis Report, including attribution, forecasts, updates and corrections.">
  <section class="section"><div class="shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">Trust & Standards</p>
    <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>
    <h2>Evidence first</h2>
    <p>We prioritize primary sources such as FAO, WFP, IPC, World Bank, national statistical agencies, agriculture ministries, climate agencies and peer-reviewed research.</p>
    <h2>Clear attribution</h2>
    <p>Claims from third parties are attributed to the source. We distinguish reporting, official estimates, projections and explanatory analysis.</p>
    <h2>Updates and corrections</h2>
    <p>Important data can change. We update articles when material evidence changes and correct material factual errors.</p>
    <h2>Reader-first SEO</h2>
    <p>Search visibility matters, but pages are written for people first. We avoid misleading headlines, duplicate country pages and content created only to capture search traffic.</p>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>
